---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import { GMM } from '../consts';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="The Searchscope crawler"
  description="What SearchscopeBot is, why it visits a website, how to recognize it, and how to allow or block it."
  headerTheme="dark"
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Crawler"
    title="The Searchscope crawler"
    lede="SearchscopeBot reads websites that their owners have connected to Searchscope. This page explains what it does, how to recognize it, and how to allow or block it."
  />

  <section class="section section--tight theme-dark">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <div class="prose reveal">
        <h2>What it does</h2>
        <p>
          SearchscopeBot visits a website when the site owner connects it to Searchscope. It fetches
          the public HTML pages, follows internal links and reads the sitemap. It records titles,
          headings, links, images, structured data (schema.org) and the page text, so the analysis
          can run. It does not log in, submit forms or fetch anything behind a password.
        </p>

        <h2>How to recognize it</h2>
        <dl class="bot-id">
          <dt>Name</dt>
          <dd>SearchscopeBot</dd>
          <dt>User agent</dt>
          <dd>SearchscopeBot/1.0 (+https://searchscope.io/bot)</dd>
          <dt>IP address</dt>
          <dd>161.35.167.82</dd>
        </dl>
        <p>Every request comes from that one IP address.</p>

        <h2>How it behaves</h2>
        <ul class="bot-list">
          <li>
            It checks robots.txt before it fetches a URL. It follows the rules for its user agent,
            including a Crawl-delay line if you set one.
          </li>
          <li>
            It makes at most 6 requests at a time, with a 0.3 second pause between requests to the
            same site. A customer can slow it down further in their settings.
          </li>
          <li>A crawl reads between about 500 and 10,000 pages, depending on the customer's plan.</li>
          <li>
            After a crawl it checks up to 100 outbound links from the site to see that they still
            work. It sends a HEAD request for each one, which asks for the headers only, not the page.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Allow it</h2>
        <p>
          If a firewall or bot protection blocks unknown crawlers, allow the IP address
          <code>161.35.167.82</code> or the user agent string above. This applies to Cloudflare,
          Sucuri, Wordfence and similar tools.
        </p>

        <h2>Block it</h2>
        <p>Add these two lines to your robots.txt:</p>
        <pre><code>User-agent: SearchscopeBot
Disallow: /</code></pre>
        <p>Or block the IP address <code>161.35.167.82</code>.</p>
        <p>
          Blocking the crawler stops the analysis for that site. The site owner then sees no findings
          from Searchscope. If someone else set up Searchscope for the site, check with them before
          you block it.
        </p>

        <h2>Content Studio</h2>
        <p>
          When a customer uses Content Studio, the same user agent fetches single public pages they
          point it at: their own page, or a competitor's page they are studying. That is one request
          per page, not a crawl.
        </p>

        <p class="prose__foot">
          Questions about the crawler? <a href="/contact">Contact us</a>. Searchscope is built and run
          by {GMM.name}.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .prose {
    max-width: 68ch;
  }
  .prose h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xs);
  }
  .prose h2:first-of-type {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .prose p {
    color: var(--ink-dim);
    font-size: var(--step-0);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-s);
  }
  .prose a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }
  .prose code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.92em;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .prose pre {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--ink);
    background: var(--surface-panel);
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: var(--radius-s);
    padding: var(--space-s) var(--space-m);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-s);
    overflow-x: auto;
    white-space: pre;
  }
  .prose pre code {
    font-size: inherit;
  }
  .bot-id {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: max-content minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 0.7rem var(--space-m);
    margin: var(--space-m) 0 var(--space-s);
    padding: var(--space-m);
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: var(--radius-s);
    background: var(--surface-panel);
  }
  .bot-id dt {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--step--2);
    font-weight: 500;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    padding-top: 0.2em;
  }
  .bot-id dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--ink);
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .bot-id {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0.15rem;
    }
    .bot-id dd {
      margin-bottom: 0.7rem;
    }
    .bot-id dd:last-child {
      margin-bottom: 0;
    }
  }
  .bot-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-s);
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.7rem;
  }
  .bot-list li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--ink-dim);
    font-size: var(--step-0);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .bot-list li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.72em;
    width: 5px;
    height: 5px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--ink-faint);
  }
  .prose__foot {
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
    padding-top: var(--space-l);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }
</style>
